{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["גור אריה יהודה — like: ״והנה כפיר אריות״. The young one is called גור, as it is written: ״בתוך כפירים רבתה גוריה״. Because it is swifter and stronger than an old lion, he likens Yehudah to a young lion." "מטרף בני עלית — you, Yehudah my son: after you go up from tearing prey among the nations and you crouch and lie down in your city, no enemy will come to startle you and raise you from your place. This is the core of its plain sense. And those who explain it in connection with the sale of Yosef did not know the plain sense of the verse at all, nor the division of accents at all."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:47:41.990708623Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}